2ed6-5ef6-5208-8e39-a3c440d5d032" :question/math-academy-id "q-74094" :question/problem "Given that $‖v‖=6$ and $u\\cdot v=-9$, find the smallest possible value of $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-9| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot 6 \\\\ 9 & \\le 6\\cdot ‖u‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le 2\\cdot ‖u‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\frac{1}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot ‖u‖ \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & \\le ‖u‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖u‖$\nis  $\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74094/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74094"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39430/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "dcfb5fc3-8825-56c8-a76a-c19f11ea1076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39430/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "39632596-f778-55ad-b2bc-1664410c519f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39430/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "cc2bf5db-aee3-5546-836e-c65c1b9b5b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39430/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "80eb29b8-3991-5560-bb52-0566e8cbaea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39430/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :ans