 $u\\cdot v=-20$ and $‖v‖=5$,  what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n|u\\cdot v|\\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $‖u‖.$ So first, we compute $‖u‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-20| & \\le \\sqrt{14+k}\\cdot (5) \\\\ 4 & \\le \\sqrt{14+k} \\\\ {4}^{2} & \\le {(\\sqrt{14+k})}^{2} \\\\ 16 & \\le 14+k \\\\ 2 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40882/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ec34a19-988a-5421-8c05-6bb4c5a9e366"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40882"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140442/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "eb52230c-c6b9-53b1-965b-2ec48ceb1af8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140442/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "092c1770-40b4-5200-acd8-d8b6fcfb42dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140442/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ae4aaa0b-f1e5-5d31-b9d0-5485760c459e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140442/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b9ef760c-9ca5-5bb8-aa91-f0f99a504f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140442/selection/68