begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\text{ }-2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula  \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{25}\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{25})≈{76.11}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40559"] :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+(-\\sqrt{5})\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 5+1\\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{5})^{2}+{7}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{\\sqrt{64}\\cdot \\sqrt{32}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{32}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566/selection/74e618ab6c0a0c8785d65d3ed39f0e4fef652059248432d44808060b15eb7f78" :answer/id #uuid "20f97160-8000-5a7f-9849-7df9ee3d0f15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{89.76}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566/selection/9021db310fd96c35273123354ca20d4cbb181f7831db229cfb48f1679eb382d3" :answer/id #uuid "cd155694-37f8-5b35-b69c-21c31fdb06af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{75.5}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566/selection/50c698632342c807d1c8e7f57503693d3c447d897ddb4e54e46adcf82c84e8cc" :answer/id #uuid "cec6eaf3-72ee-5a46-a542-7c32b3c2ad35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{72.25}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566/selection/3a21e4c41348b3e85d7c2552d725952c3686001567bc246466456dae6aa4c1d0" :answer/id #uuid "e94f67e0-c2fb-5e1c-b8e1-4210b9161a00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{82.34}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566/selection/2c24b48b045e4304281d126802c8472cdc02d11ecb6664e3035f8caa19bb098b" :answer/id #uuid "03a177b7-fe3f-59eb-8755-0b71633739db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{70.76}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb716df0-c0ac-5805-80b2-66451d4dad0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40566/selection/2c24b48b045e4304281d126802c8472cdc02d11ecb6664e3035f8caa19bb098b" :answer-field/choices ["q-40566/selection/74e618ab6c0a0c8785d65d3ed39f0e4fef652059248432d44808060b15eb7f78" "q-40566/selection/9021db310fd96c35273123354ca20d4cbb181f7831db229cfb48f1679eb382d3" "q-40566/selection/50c698632342c807d1c8e7f57503693d3c447d897ddb4e54e46adcf82c84e8cc" "q-40566/selection/3a21e4c41348b3e85d7c2552d725952c3686001567bc246466456dae6aa4c1d0" "q-40566/selection/2c24b48b045e4304281d126802c8472cdc02d11ecb6664e3035f8caa19bb098b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40566" :question/id #uuid "1189bfdd-553b-5a47-a40b-2ac3c101817d" :question/math-academy-id "q-40566" :question/problem "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors  $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\text{ }1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot (-5)+5\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-5)^{2}}\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{67}\\sqrt{55}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3685}})≈{70.76}^{∘}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40566/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6bde92b0-4e98-5c2e-848e-7a5febc848ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40566"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456/selection/a9a4468136aac72cedaab6e1a2a0d2752ed26a2f96f4ff1355e702dcb9255894" :answer/id #uuid "5d5eee5a-707a-5466-92b1-0989f3be06ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{75}{14\\sqrt{30}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456/selection/7610d54e389a12846c30d9831c1ddc419b6a897a91f6c2413dc5356e8f51ed35" :answer/id #uuid "71cd5b1b-2599-5755-b620-3dc575e9b467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{30}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456/selection/05e4212d3670f35da094646450f272ba9ce174b4cfe6826febaac401fe4b929e" :answer/id #uuid "a6f75180-9d09-5b40-8b2b-4fc32df56efd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456/selection/54bccb6e7fa5985fecaea6f6887d4b4bd8ceea068492913de461e612de81788a" :answer/id #uuid "86c2855f-bcb8-51da-b62a-919cf201330d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{30}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456/selection/1c9023b5cddfa20d82dbf48b14bf6001180899b81ffcce04e869f45d13aacc80" :answer/id #uuid "f0f3aa12-6aad-55da-a7fb-de00dae1736a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{7\\sqrt{30}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "78bb470b-f267-5720-a815-7921706cd0ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140456/selection/05e4212d3670f35da094646450f272ba9ce174b4cfe6826febaac401fe4b929e" :answer-field/choices ["q-140456/selection/a9a4468136aac72cedaab6e1a2a0d2752ed26a2f96f4ff1355e702dcb9255894" "q-140456/selection/7610d54e389a12846c30d9831c1ddc419b6a897a91f6c2413dc5356e8f51ed35" "q-140456/selection/05e4212d3670f35da094646450f272ba9ce174b4cfe6826febaac401fe4b929e" "q-140456/selection/54bccb6e7fa5985fecaea6f6887d4b4bd8ceea068492913de461e612de81788a" "q-140456/selection/1c9023b5cddfa20d82dbf48b14bf6001180899b81ffcce04e869f45d13aacc80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140456" :question/id #uuid "ab53b11a-f41d-5f0a-ae52-61c8789440eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-140456" :question/problem "Let $A(1,1,-1,-1)$, $B(2,4,6,8)$, and $C(1,2,3,4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 4+9\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{7}^{2}+{9}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{5}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{\\sqrt{140}\\cdot \\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{2\\sqrt{35}\\cdot \\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{76}{14\\sqrt{30}} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{7\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140456/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "ef6d5d0c-0dc1-542d-842d-b2ca3374ae1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121/selection/92b01a396921f1e31b0533170c5f39c791e7a40e69e72c8e62397697afa08933" :answer/id #uuid "144a34ba-5eda-59f1-9877-014e1af19dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121/selection/2faeea9c9eedefeae671c807b51ede422449e2976700bcbd604b58e50a79be38" :answer/id #uuid "a005dabc-8c9e-5ce5-bef1-52cc88152338" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121/selection/261b86b9a4ece8c8bb6b2a712b25cb85f6503ebccec3a40aa209961563450bfc" :answer/id #uuid "84ee6a9f-71e6-596e-a48b-1715ddc127c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{23}{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121/selection/5e126195aedcde422663d5931fffe1578adcd4994ff1c5a1a90c6bbedf19c0ce" :answer/id #uuid "e663d1dd-6442-560d-b0dc-cfd9be4290df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{23}{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d44d428-2a6c-5ae2-b39d-fbccca778fc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74121/selection/5e126195aedcde422663d5931fffe1578adcd4994ff1c5a1a90c6bbedf19c0ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-74121/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-74121/selection/92b01a396921f1e31b0533170c5f39c791e7a40e69e72c8e62397697afa08933" "q-74121/selection/2faeea9c9eedefeae671c807b51ede422449e2976700bcbd604b58e50a79be38" "q-74121/selection/261b86b9a4ece8c8bb6b2a712b25cb85f6503ebccec3a40aa209961563450bfc" "q-74121/selection/5e126195aedcde422663d5931fffe1578adcd4994ff1c5a1a90c6bbedf19c0ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74121" :question/id #uuid "b80ce80c-769f-5a27-bb3a-0f2b90a90e8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74121" :question/problem "Let $A(-1,3,2,-4)$, $B(1,0,1,-2)$, and $C(0,1,-1,2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 6}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{\\sqrt{18}\\cdot \\sqrt{50}} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-74121/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74121"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455/selection/dc33de0369d86fa1a57047316fabd3b05149ddc42c0a4c39ff26d583b2fb1595" :answer/id #uuid "31f41a8a-ba68-5d70-a6b1-f961dfbefa5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{22}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455/selection/56ccf721b60d7740517079d51bf8a976f8cdd9488763f618ce3aaebe673f6aca" :answer/id #uuid "5fd2e6ca-32f8-53e1-b1b4-8628a23b2ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455/selection/1ed95fb008c6587562a19e6612592e62b29df50b5b0579c2c9b2d12a2e01bfe4" :answer/id #uuid "8838e5fa-5f97-5a64-bc47-bfa4b7983c83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455/selection/48de2ac45156b1ac62d6b496dd2657eec432ca281413929bf47145361ff2cf0b" :answer/id #uuid "51996b6c-222d-5450-abdf-f041d8ccc81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{132}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455/selection/9711161a51ee99ff99ae7a375e03fe6ecd3a6151d15d24e0cdee6ba4f398daed" :answer/id #uuid "1f934f6f-6e95-57c5-a7d1-28ea6070e152" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{22}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffdc6b88-736f-50db-9d3b-df2b11e520c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140455/selection/56ccf721b60d7740517079d51bf8a976f8cdd9488763f618ce3aaebe673f6aca" :answer-field/choices ["q-140455/selection/dc33de0369d86fa1a57047316fabd3b05149ddc42c0a4c39ff26d583b2fb1595" "q-140455/selection/56ccf721b60d7740517079d51bf8a976f8cdd9488763f618ce3aaebe673f6aca" "q-140455/selection/1ed95fb008c6587562a19e6612592e62b29df50b5b0579c2c9b2d12a2e01bfe4" "q-140455/selection/48de2ac45156b1ac62d6b496dd2657eec432ca281413929bf47145361ff2cf0b" "q-140455/selection/9711161a51ee99ff99ae7a375e03fe6ecd3a6151d15d24e0cdee6ba4f398daed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140455" :question/id #uuid "41b261c3-9f5f-5508-8cac-5fa8af188eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-140455" :question/problem "Let $A(1,0,-1,2)$ and $B(4,8,2,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 4+0\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{88}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{132}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140455/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40886"] :question/problem "Let $A(1,-1,2,0)$, $B(1,0,0,-1)$, and $C(0,1,1,0).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠BAC.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $v=\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $w=\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =b-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =c-a \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $\\theta =m∠BAC$ be the angle between the vectors $v$ and $w.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "e9b3e6ed-94a6-585d-b2af-97fbb973d4b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "ba1afbb6-da0f-5a21-9e5f-a3528ce59a45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105/selection/a9805d3e0ad2e1ed850c9e7bd9ca69f0f8a3163035c09d70f8cfad4e162f2103" :answer/id #uuid "80cc14f2-f4c0-5c9e-8022-b0dea30544d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "f95114cb-bd98-5724-8197-61a54eb833f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "3af8684e-74bd-55cd-bae3-3c9ffdcf6002" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bc80040-c640-59c4-b2be-d78308936881" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74105/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-74105/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-74105/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-74105/selection/a9805d3e0ad2e1ed850c9e7bd9ca69f0f8a3163035c09d70f8cfad4e162f2103" "q-74105/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-74105/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74105" :question/id #uuid "97251e19-2588-52aa-ba2e-6f2b81a48ba1" :question/math-academy-id "q-74105" :question/problem "Let $A(1,-3,2,-1)$ and $B(1,1,3,-2).$ Find the cosine of the angle $∠AOB$, where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta =m∠AOB$ be the angle between the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Then, we can find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{15}\\cdot \\sqrt{15}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{6÷3}{15÷3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74105/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b56b45b-94dd-5ba1-aae6-6b17cffaf532"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5554"] :question/problem "Consider the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/d1a095e61e6ea64f97a105fd69bc07f3f44990cd6d9794e54e355463c37a2413.png) Given that $\\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v}=-12$ and $\\Vert \\mathbf{v}\\Vert =4,$ what is the smallest possible value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality,\n\n$$\n\\vert \\mathbf{u}\\cdot \\mathbf{v} \\vert \\leq \\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{v} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nWe are given all the quantities in the inequality above, except for $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert.$ So first, we compute $\\Vert \\mathbf{u} \\Vert$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{k})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-12| & \\le \\sqrt{6+k}\\cdot (4) \\\\ 12 & \\le 4\\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ 3 & \\le \\sqrt{6+k} \\\\ {3}^{2} & \\le (\\sqrt{6+k})^{2} \\\\ 9 & \\le 6+k \\\\ 3 & \\le k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $k$ is $3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5555"] :question/problem "Find the acute angle between the vectors ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/5ed21f4bb536757026315cce838f4cc3028493adac2ff29d46a5b8cbdf11170b.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14046175/assets/8d813e104a708be37ba44b9448806f49ea21a16fe7f613314d2eeab2b59bbda2.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos\\theta = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{w}}{\\Vert\\mathbf{v}\\Vert \\, \\Vert \\mathbf{w}\\Vert},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-2)\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta=\\arccos \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right)=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5910"] :question/problem "Let $A(-2, 4, -2, 2)$ and $B(4, 0, -1, -4).$ Find the cosine of the angle $\\angle{AOB},$ where $O(0,0,0,0)$ is the origin." :question/worked-solution "First, let\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=\\overset{\\to }{OA}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=\\overset{\\to }{OB}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, let $\\theta = m\\angle{AOB}$ be the angle between the vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}.$ Then, we can find $\\cos \\theta$ using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{‖a‖\\,‖b‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{1}{b}_{1}+{a}_{2}{b}_{2}+{a}_{3}{b}_{3}+{a}_{4}{b}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2}+{b}_{3}^{2}+{b}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\,\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{28}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-14}{\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{33}} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{33}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
